
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D F G : Points
AB = BD [00]
AB ⟂ BD [01]
C,F,B are collinear [02]
AF ⟂ BC [03]
GA = BC [04]
G,A,F are collinear [05]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
E : Points
AB ∥ DE [06]

 * Proof steps:
001. C,F,B are collinear [02] & G,A,F are collinear [05] & BC ⟂ AF [03] ⇒  CF ⟂ GA [07]
002. AB ⟂ BD [01] & AB ∥ DE [06] ⇒  BD ⟂ ED [08]
003. CF ⟂ GA [07] & BD ⟂ ED [08] ⇒  ∠(CF-BD) = ∠(GA-ED) [09]
004. CF ⟂ GA [07] & BD ⟂ ED [08] ⇒  ∠(CF-ED) = ∠(GA-BD) [10]
005. G,A,F are collinear [05] & ∠(CF-BD) = ∠(GA-ED) [09] & C,F,B are collinear [02] & AB ∥ DE [06] ⇒  ∠BAG = ∠DBC [11]
006. AB = BD [00] & GA = BC [04] & ∠BAG = ∠DBC [11] (SAS)⇒  ∠BGA = ∠DCB [12]
007. AB = BD [00] & GA = BC [04] & ∠BAG = ∠DBC [11] (SAS)⇒  ∠ABD = ∠(BG-CD) [13]
008. ∠BGA = ∠DCB [12] & G,A,F are collinear [05] & ∠(CF-ED) = ∠(GA-BD) [10] & C,F,B are collinear [02] & AB ∥ DE [06] & ∠ABD = ∠(BG-CD) [13] ⇒  GB ⟂ CD
==========================
